Set up Copilot — Step 2: Repository configuration for the Copilot coding agent
Purpose

Provide a repository-level configuration that the Copilot coding agent can use to understand how to build, test, and run this project and what to avoid or keep private.
Overview

Add two artifacts:
A machine-readable config file (.github/copilot-agent.yml) with commands, ignore paths, and repository metadata.
A human-readable instructions file (this file) describing what the config contains and why.
Recommended config (example)

Add the following YAML to .github/copilot-agent.yml. Adjust commands, branch and package manager to match this repository.
# .github/copilot-agent.yml
name: "LFASProtocol Copilot agent config"
version: 1

# Workspace and branch
workspace_root: "."
default_branch: "main"        # change to your repo's default branch if different

# Tooling / commands
package_manager: "npm"        # or "pnpm", "yarn", "maven", "pip", etc.
install_command: "npm ci"
build_command: "npm run build"
test_command: "npm test --silent"
start_command: "npm start"

# Devcontainer / reproducible dev environment (optional)
dev_container: ".devcontainer"   # path if you provide one

# Paths and files to exclude from agent operations
exclude_paths:
  - "node_modules"
  - "dist"
  - "build"
  - ".venv"
  - ".git"

# Files / directories treated as sensitive (do NOT attempt to read or return contents)
sensitive_paths:
  - ".env"
  - ".secrets"
  - "credentials.json"
  - "private_keys/**"

# Repo-level context, helpful for the agent and maintainers
repo_context:
  description: "LFAS v4.1 KG PROMPT ENGINE"
  owner: "LFASProtocol"
  contact: "maintainers@lfasprotocol.org"

# Pull request defaults for agent-created PRs
pull_request:
  default_labels:
    - "automation:copilot"
    - "area:devops"
  pr_template: ".github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md"

# Onboarding notes for human reviewers
onboarding_notes: |
  - The agent should run `npm ci` and `npm test` before opening changes.
  - Avoid editing files under `knowledge_graph/` unless the change includes tests and a data-migration plan.
  - For schema or KG changes, reference the KG governance doc at docs/kg-governance.md
